<?jelly escape-by-default='true'?>
<div>
    Integrates Jenkins pipelines with the Harness platform via the Harness CLI (<code>hc</code>).

    <p>This plugin provides pipeline steps:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <b>hc</b> — Runs any Harness CLI command directly from a pipeline step.
            The CLI binary is automatically downloaded from GitHub releases and installed on the agent.
            Authentication (<code>hc auth login</code>) is handled automatically once per build
            using the API token configured under <i>Manage Jenkins → Configure System → Harness CLI Configuration</i>.
        </li>
        <!-- Uncomment below li section too when , HarnessBuildInfoPublisher.java and HarnessBuildInfoStep.java is uncommented  -->
        <!-- li>
            <b>publishHarnessBuildInfo</b> — Collects Jenkins build metadata (job details, git info,
            trigger causes, agent labels, pipeline stage) and publishes it to the build log.
            Adds a sidebar link on the build page that opens the Harness Artifact Registry for the configured registry.
        </li-->
    </ul>

    <p>
        The Harness CLI tool installation is managed under <i>Manage Jenkins → Tools → Harness CLI installations</i>,
        where you can pin a specific CLI version or leave it blank to always use the latest GitHub release.
    </p>
</div>
